      "claim": "Measured human oral bioavailability for small polar polyhydroxy compounds supports F >= 20%: mannitol ~20-22.8% (C01, C06, C09, C17), glucose 0.722-0.843 or 38% (C10, C15, C16), sorbitol 0.36-0.38 (C03, C19), and propylene glycol very high/close to complete (C13, C28, C29).",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C06","C09","C17","C10","C15","C16","C03","C19","C13","C28","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 mannitol exposure records show dose-linear Cmax and AUC after 50-150 g oral doses, consistent with meaningful oral absorption rather than negligible exposure.",
      "card_ids": ["C35","C36","C37","C38","C40","C41","C42","C43","C45","C46"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4/L5 mannitol Caco-2 records show very low apparent permeability and no net efflux (C59, C62, C65, C68, C69), yet mannitol still reaches about 20% human F; low permeability and absence of efflux are therefore not affirmative evidence for F < 20% in this small polar molecule class.",
      "card_ids": ["C59","C62","C65","C68","C69","C01","C06"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance and metabolic stability records concern warfarin, acenocoumarol, GSK6, BDB, DON, and nebivolol; none is ascorbic acid and none provides direct or transferable threshold-relevant oral bioavailability evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct ascorbic acid absolute oral bioavailability or matched oral/IV AUC record is present in the supplied cards.",
    "No direct ascorbic acid hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement is present; L6 records are for unrelated molecules.",
    "Active transport (SVCT1/2) contribution to ascorbic acid absorption is inferred from the query prior, not from a measured record.",
    "Dose dependence and saturation of ascorbic acid absorption are not captured.",
    "Transfer from mannitol/glucose/sorbitol/propylene glycol contexts is qualitative; species, doses, and patient status differ."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) maintained with moderate confidence. Small polar polyhydroxy compounds with measured human F at or above threshold, dose-linear mannitol exposure, and the absence of affirmative low-F evidence support the prediction. L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic stability records are for unrelated molecules and do not provide ascorbic acid-specific evidence for F < 20%."
}

